WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.055 --> 00:00:07.157
The next day Pollyanna went to Sunday school after the church service.

2
00:00:07.158 --> 00:00:13.799
As she started to walk home, she spotted Dr. Chilton. He offered her a ride.

3
00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:20.964
"Mr. Pendleton wants you to visit him this afternoon," Dr. Chilton said as Pollyanna settled into the carriage.

4
00:00:20.965 --> 00:00:23.827
"He said it was very important."

5
00:00:23.828 --> 00:00:28.136
Pollyanna nodded. "Yes, I'll be there."

6
00:00:28.137 --> 00:00:31.587
"You seemed to upset my patient yesterday."

7
00:00:31.588 --> 00:00:37.457
The doctor's eyes twinkled. "I'm not sure you should go after all."

8
00:00:37.458 --> 00:00:44.489
Pollyanna laughed. "Oh, it wasn't me. It was Aunt Polly."

9
00:00:44.490 --> 00:00:47.647
"Your aunt!" Dr. Chilton said.

10
00:00:47.648 --> 00:00:49.900
Pollyanna bounced on the seat.

11
00:00:49.901 --> 00:00:54.630
"It's so exciting, just like a story in a book.

12
00:00:54.631 --> 00:00:59.781
Mr. Pendleton said not to mention it, but he won't mind if you know.

13
00:00:59.782 --> 00:01:03.162
He meant I shouldn't mention it to Aunt Polly.

14
00:01:03.163 --> 00:01:07.870
Of course, he'll want to tell her himself because that's what sweethearts do."

15
00:01:07.871 --> 00:01:16.346
"Sweethearts!" At that word the horse started violently, as if Dr. Chilton had jerked the reins.

16
00:01:16.347 --> 00:01:21.565
"Yes, Nancy told me that Aunt Polly had a sweetheart years ago.

17
00:01:21.566 --> 00:01:25.323
But they quarreled and broke off their engagement.

18
00:01:25.324 --> 00:01:31.990
We just figured out who Aunt Polly's sweetheart is. It's Mr. Pendleton!"

19
00:01:31.991 --> 00:01:38.521
"Really? I hadn't heard that." Dr. Chilton looked amused.

20
00:01:38.522 --> 00:01:43.000
They were almost at the Harrington house, so Pollyanna hurried to finish.

21
00:01:43.001 --> 00:01:50.735
"I'm so glad now. Everything has turned out perfectly just like in a book.

22
00:01:50.736 --> 00:01:53.902
Mr. Pendleton asked me to come live with him.

23
00:01:53.903 --> 00:01:58.254
But I can't leave Aunt Polly after all she's done for me.

24
00:01:58.255 --> 00:02:03.857
Then he told me about the woman he used to love and that he still loves her.

25
00:02:03.858 --> 00:02:08.632
So Aunt Polly and I will go live with him, or he'll come live with us."

26
00:02:08.633 --> 00:02:11.974
Pollyanna paused for breath.

27
00:02:11.975 --> 00:02:18.137
"We haven't got everything settled yet, so I suppose that's why he wants to see me later."

28
00:02:18.138 --> 00:02:26.972
"Hmm, yes, well, here we are at your house." Dr. Chilton pulled his horse to a stop.

29
00:02:26.973 --> 00:02:36.008
"There's Aunt Polly in the window!" Pollyanna cried. "Oh, now I don't see her."

30
00:02:36.009 --> 00:02:43.635
The doctor was no longer smiling.

31
00:02:43.636 --> 00:02:49.019
That afternoon Pollyanna found a nervous Mr. Pendleton waiting in his library.

32
00:02:49.020 --> 00:02:53.766
"I've been thinking about this ever since you left yesterday," he said.

33
00:02:53.767 --> 00:02:58.868
"Why did you say I wanted Aunt Polly's hand and heart years ago?"

34
00:02:58.869 --> 00:03:05.645
"Because you were sweethearts! And I was so glad you still felt that way."

35
00:03:05.646 --> 00:03:09.281
"Sweethearts? Your aunt and me?"

36
00:03:09.282 --> 00:03:16.207
Pollyanna was startled by the surprise in his voice. "Nancy said you were."

37
00:03:16.208 --> 00:03:18.771
"Nancy was wrong."

38
00:03:18.772 --> 00:03:23.674
"You mean, you weren't engaged?" Pollyanna said with dismay.

39
00:03:23.675 --> 00:03:28.631
"Never." Mr. Pendleton stared out the window.

40
00:03:28.632 --> 00:03:34.121
"But everything was working out perfectly just like in a book."

41
00:03:34.122 --> 00:03:37.193
Pollyanna was on the verge of tears.

42
00:03:37.194 --> 00:03:42.718
"I'd have been glad to live here—with Aunt Polly."

43
00:03:42.719 --> 00:03:45.963
Mr. Pendleton didn't look at Pollyanna.

44
00:03:45.964 --> 00:03:48.781
"Does that mean you won't come now?"

45
00:03:48.782 --> 00:03:53.014
"I can't. I'm Aunt Polly's."

46
00:03:53.015 --> 00:03:59.945
The man turned toward Pollyanna and said fiercely, "Before you were hers, you were your mother's.

47
00:03:59.946 --> 00:04:04.118
And it was your mother's hand and heart that I wanted years ago."

48
00:04:04.119 --> 00:04:08.830
"My mother's?" Pollyanna blinked.

49
00:04:08.831 --> 00:04:12.485
She couldn't believe what she was hearing.

50
00:04:12.486 --> 00:04:16.276
"I loved your mother, but she didn't love me.

51
00:04:16.277 --> 00:04:21.380
Instead she married your father, and my whole world collapsed.

52
00:04:21.381 --> 00:04:27.558
I became a grumpy, unlovable, unloved old man—although I'm not yet sixty.

53
00:04:27.559 --> 00:04:33.714
Then one day you danced into this gray, stone house like a colorful prism.

54
00:04:33.715 --> 00:04:38.646
At first, I couldn't stand to be reminded of your mother, but that's changed.

55
00:04:38.647 --> 00:04:42.481
Now I'm begging you to let me adopt you."

56
00:04:42.482 --> 00:04:46.064
Pollyanna's eyes blurred with tears.

57
00:04:46.065 --> 00:04:51.577
"But, Mr. Pendleton, what about Aunt Polly?"

58
00:04:51.578 --> 00:04:54.661
Mr. Pendleton gestured impatiently.

59
00:04:54.662 --> 00:04:57.992
"What about me? How can I be glad without you?

60
00:04:57.993 --> 00:05:01.788
I'll spend every last cent of my money on your happiness."

61
00:05:01.789 --> 00:05:08.853
Pollyanna looked shocked. "But you've saved your money for the orphans overseas."

62
00:05:08.854 --> 00:05:10.474
"I never . . ."

63
00:05:10.475 --> 00:05:14.698
Pollyanna didn't notice that Mr. Pendleton had tried to speak.

64
00:05:14.699 --> 00:05:21.196
"And you make people like Mrs. Snow and Nancy glad with your gifts," she went on.

65
00:05:21.197 --> 00:05:23.660
Mr. Pendleton shook his head.

66
00:05:23.661 --> 00:05:26.887
"Prisms and a gold coin—they're nothing.

67
00:05:26.888 --> 00:05:30.920
And Miss Polly doesn't need you as much as I do."

68
00:05:30.921 --> 00:05:33.552
"I know she's glad—"

69
00:05:33.553 --> 00:05:36.688
"Miss Polly doesn't know how to be glad about anything.

70
00:05:36.689 --> 00:05:43.303
She only knows how to do her duty. Please, just ask if she'll let you live here."

71
00:05:43.304 --> 00:05:49.914
Pollyanna promised to ask, but she wasn't very glad about it!

